**RED (reproduction):** The CI run 38513191558/job 115686105445 IS the reproduction: first `evaluateInServiceWorker` of the run → `CdpException(Runtime.evaluate): Uncaught ReferenceError: chrome is not defined`. Locally I can also demonstrate the race window exists by attaching to a cold worker and evaluating immediately — but it's timing-dependent; I won't claim a deterministic local repro. Instead, my GREEN verification is the full integration suite locally + CI on the pushed head.

Hmm, actually — let me try ONE thing to get closer to a repro: run the ac_bridge_e2e_test suite locally BEFORE the fix to confirm the baseline passes locally (i.e., the failure is load-dependent, establishing that my change isn't fixing a deterministic bug). That's useful evidence and validates my local harness works. But building the extension is required first (`scripts/build_browser_ext.sh` — compiles dart2js, needs dart; may take a while). The suite also needs the build only for sw/agent.js (embedded agent) — ac_bridge tests use bridge + sw, maybe not the agent. The build script compiles dart2js which could take minutes. Run it in background.

